figurations:** `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]` and the C has no `#ifdef`, so there is exactly one feature combination — but I treated `dev` and `release` as distinct configurations, which turned out to matter. All 4 rows pass.\n\n**Two real bugs found and fixed** (in the Rust build config, never the C):\n\n1. **`debug-assertions` turned C's `SIGSEGV` into Rust's `SIGABRT`.** For `add_task(NULL,…)`, `print_tasks(NULL)`, `destroy_task_manager(NULL)`, `driver(NULL)` and `tasks==NULL`, the C dereferences and dies with signal 11 and empty stderr; the Rust `.so` instead panicked with `null pointer dereference occurred` and aborted (signal 6, 266 bytes of stderr). Fixed by disabling `debug-assertions`/`overflow-checks` in every profile; causality was proven by rebuilding with `-Cdebug-assertions=on` (reproduces the abort) and off again (restores parity).\n\n2. **`cargo test` never built the artifact under test.** A `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`-only lib can't be linked by test targets, so Cargo skipped emitting the `.so` entirely — my early passes were silently reusing a *stale* `.so` from an earlier `cargo build`, which is exactly what produced one misleading result mid-investigation. Fixed by adding `rlib` (the tests still only ever `dlopen`) and by making the harness pick the most recently modified of `deps/` vs the uplifted copy.\n\nNotable coverage details: the null-dereference rows are compared by **termination signal** in a re-executed child process, and the four `malloc`-failure rows (including `driver`'s per-line allocation) are **genuinely reached** via `RLIMIT_AS` clamping plus heap exhaustion — confirmed by the resulting `[ERROR] Failed to allocate memory for …` records rather than assumed. Two harness pitfalls were also fixed: libtest's own progress lines leaking into captured `stdout` (one serialized `#[test]` per file), and LLVM deleting the unused `malloc` in the exhaustion loop at `opt-level=2` (infinite loop in release).\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified apart from creating the documented `build/` directory.","ttft_ms":2526,"ttft_stream_ms":2364,"time_to_request_ms":35,"type":"result","duration_ms":3440574,"uuid":"79c3cf8a-c375-41dc-9490-f59df2618f81"}
